<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Guides on kevin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/</link><description>Recent content in Guides on kevin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Proxy and egress</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/proxy-and-egress/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/proxy-and-egress/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="proxy-and-egress"&gt;Proxy and egress&lt;a class="anchor" href="#proxy-and-egress"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;kevin does not change files on your machine, such as &lt;code&gt;/etc/hosts&lt;/code&gt;. You reach the services of an environment through the kevin proxy.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="set-the-proxy-and-console-addresses"&gt;Set the proxy and console addresses&lt;a class="anchor" href="#set-the-proxy-and-console-addresses"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every environment file sets both addresses:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;proxy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;127.0.0.1:18080&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;gateway_port&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;18082&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;127.0.0.1:18081&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;gateway_port&lt;/code&gt; is the port that containers use to reach the proxy. Choose ports that are free on your machine. kevin does not choose them for you, so the addresses stay the same across runs.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Trust the kevin CA</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/ca-and-trust/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/ca-and-trust/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="trust-the-kevin-ca"&gt;Trust the kevin CA&lt;a class="anchor" href="#trust-the-kevin-ca"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The kevin proxy serves HTTPS with certificates signed by a local CA. Until your machine trusts that CA, clients reject the certificates, and &lt;code&gt;curl&lt;/code&gt; needs &lt;code&gt;--cacert ~/.kevin/root.crt&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="install-the-root-ca"&gt;Install the root CA&lt;a class="anchor" href="#install-the-root-ca"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin ca install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do this once per machine. It does not need a project, and it covers every kevin project.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;kevin adds the root CA to:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The macOS keychain, or the Linux CA directory, for your user.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The certificate database of each Firefox profile.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;macOS asks you to confirm the change.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Kubernetes clusters</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/kubernetes/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/kubernetes/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="kubernetes-clusters"&gt;Kubernetes clusters&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kubernetes-clusters"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This guide adds a local Kubernetes cluster to an environment with &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/steps/kubernetes/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;builtin:kubernetes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="prerequisites"&gt;Prerequisites&lt;a class="anchor" href="#prerequisites"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kubectl&lt;/code&gt; on your &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The command of your driver on your &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; driver, &lt;code&gt;k3d&lt;/code&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;k3d&lt;/code&gt; driver, &lt;code&gt;minikube&lt;/code&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;minikube&lt;/code&gt; driver.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="add-a-cluster"&gt;Add a cluster&lt;a class="anchor" href="#add-a-cluster"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cluster&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:kubernetes&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;driver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;kind&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;egress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;docker.io&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;*.docker.io&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;*.docker.com&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;egress&lt;/code&gt; lists the registries that the nodes pull images from when &lt;code&gt;proxy.egress.deny&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;. Pods and containers in the environment reach each other by name.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Deploying workloads</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/deploying-workloads/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/deploying-workloads/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="deploying-workloads"&gt;Deploying workloads&lt;a class="anchor" href="#deploying-workloads"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This guide deploys into a cluster from a &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/steps/kubernetes/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;builtin:kubernetes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; step. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/kubernetes/"&gt;Kubernetes clusters&lt;/a&gt; to add one.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="prerequisites"&gt;Prerequisites&lt;a class="anchor" href="#prerequisites"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kubectl&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;helm&lt;/code&gt; for Helm charts, on your &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="apply-manifests"&gt;Apply manifests&lt;a class="anchor" href="#apply-manifests"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add a &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/steps/kubectl/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;builtin:kubectl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; step that reads the cluster&amp;rsquo;s kubeconfig:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:kubectl&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;cluster&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kubeconfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${needs.cluster.out.kubeconfig}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${needs.cluster.out.context}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;k8s/app.yaml&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Set one of:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;manifest&lt;/code&gt;: YAML in the environment file.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt;: a manifest file or directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kustomize&lt;/code&gt;: a kustomization directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A relative path resolves against the project directory.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Intercept a hostname</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/intercept-hostnames/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/intercept-hostnames/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="intercept-a-hostname"&gt;Intercept a hostname&lt;a class="anchor" href="#intercept-a-hostname"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This guide sends traffic for a real hostname to a local service, with no change to the code that calls it. The example replaces Amazon S3 with &lt;a href="https://ministack.org/"&gt;MiniStack&lt;/a&gt;, a local AWS emulator.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="start-the-local-service"&gt;Start the local service&lt;a class="anchor" href="#start-the-local-service"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fake_s3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;ministackorg/ministack&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;s3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;port&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;4566&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fake_s3_ready&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:wait&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;fake_s3&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;timeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;15s&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;http://${needs.fake_s3.out.host_4566}/&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;wait&lt;/code&gt; step makes the route start only after the service answers HTTP requests.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="add-intercept-routes"&gt;Add intercept routes&lt;a class="anchor" href="#add-intercept-routes"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s3_intercept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:route&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;fake_s3&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;fake_s3_ready&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;host&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${needs.fake_s3.out.host_4566}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;intercept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;host&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;*.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${needs.fake_s3.out.host_4566}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;intercept&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;With &lt;code&gt;intercept: true&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;host&lt;/code&gt; is the full hostname, not a name on the environment domain. S3 clients use both the regional host and a subdomain for each bucket, so the example routes both.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Third-party plugins</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/third-party-plugins/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/third-party-plugins/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="third-party-plugins"&gt;Third-party plugins&lt;a class="anchor" href="#third-party-plugins"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A third-party plugin adds step types that kevin does not ship. You can find plugins in an index, a git repository that lists plugins and their releases.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="add-an-index"&gt;Add an index&lt;a class="anchor" href="#add-an-index"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin plugin index add https://github.com/acme/kevin-plugin-index&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;kevin clones the repository and prints the number of plugins it found. The index gets an alias derived from the URL. To choose the alias, add &lt;code&gt;--as &amp;lt;alias&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To see your indexes, run &lt;code&gt;kevin plugin index list&lt;/code&gt;. To get new releases, run &lt;code&gt;kevin plugin index update&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Per-machine and per-run settings</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/local-and-per-run-settings/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/local-and-per-run-settings/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="per-machine-and-per-run-settings"&gt;Per-machine and per-run settings&lt;a class="anchor" href="#per-machine-and-per-run-settings"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Both tasks use CUE package mode: the environment file starts with a &lt;code&gt;package&lt;/code&gt; clause, and kevin loads every &lt;code&gt;.cue&lt;/code&gt; file in the directory with the same clause as one environment.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="keep-machine-specific-values-out-of-source-control"&gt;Keep machine-specific values out of source control&lt;a class="anchor" href="#keep-machine-specific-values-out-of-source-control"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add a package clause to the top of &lt;code&gt;kevin.cue&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kevin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add a local file to &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;kevin.local.cue&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &amp;gt;&amp;gt; .gitignore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Put the machine-specific values in &lt;code&gt;kevin.local.cue&lt;/code&gt;, with the same package clause:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kevin&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;local-dev-token&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Check the result:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;</description></item><item><title>Relay settings</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/relay-settings/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/relay-settings/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="relay-settings"&gt;Relay settings&lt;a class="anchor" href="#relay-settings"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every environment runs a relay container on the project network. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/concepts/relay/"&gt;Relay&lt;/a&gt; for what it does.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="reach-a-container-port-without-publishing-it"&gt;Reach a container port without publishing it&lt;a class="anchor" href="#reach-a-container-port-without-publishing-it"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Each &lt;code&gt;expose&lt;/code&gt; entry of a &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/steps/container/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;builtin:container&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; step normally uses a host port. To reach the port through the relay instead, set &lt;code&gt;relay: true&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;postgres:16&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;postgres&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;port&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;5432&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;relay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The step&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;forward_postgres&lt;/code&gt; system value is a &lt;code&gt;127.0.0.1:&amp;lt;port&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; address. The console shows it. Any client can connect to it:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Variables</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/variables/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/variables/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="variables"&gt;Variables&lt;a class="anchor" href="#variables"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="declare-a-variable"&gt;Declare a variable&lt;a class="anchor" href="#declare-a-variable"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add a &lt;code&gt;variables&lt;/code&gt; block to &lt;code&gt;kevin.cue&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;variables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;region&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;us-east-1&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Omit &lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt; to make the variable required.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Read it in a &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; block:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;REGION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${vars.region}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Check the result:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="declare-a-typed-variable"&gt;Declare a typed variable&lt;a class="anchor" href="#declare-a-typed-variable"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add a &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; constraint alongside (or instead of) &lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt;. See the &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/environment-file/#variables"&gt;&lt;code&gt;#Variable&lt;/code&gt; field table&lt;/a&gt; for the CUE expressions &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; accepts:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;variables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;replicas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;env_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;prod&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;staging&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;dev&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;dev&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;strict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A variable with no &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; is a plain string.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Read it the same way, in any field the plugin&amp;rsquo;s own schema types to match:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;replicas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;${vars.replicas}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Check the result:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A value outside the declared constraint fails validation with the constraint it violated.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rerun on change</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/rerun-on-change/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/rerun-on-change/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="rerun-on-change"&gt;Rerun on change&lt;a class="anchor" href="#rerun-on-change"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="watch-a-directory"&gt;Watch a directory&lt;a class="anchor" href="#watch-a-directory"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add &lt;code&gt;watch&lt;/code&gt; to the step. Each entry is a file or directory in the project directory:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:exec&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;watch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;src/&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;up&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;command&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;make&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;build&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Start the environment:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Save a file under &lt;code&gt;src/&lt;/code&gt;. kevin logs &lt;code&gt;change in src/main.go, rerunning&lt;/code&gt; for the step and reruns it, along with the steps that depend on it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="validate-the-paths"&gt;Validate the paths&lt;a class="anchor" href="#validate-the-paths"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;kevin validate&lt;/code&gt;. It fails if a watched path does not exist, is absolute, or leaves the project directory. See the &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/environment-file/#steps"&gt;&lt;code&gt;watch&lt;/code&gt; field&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Build an image</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/build-images/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/build-images/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="build-an-image"&gt;Build an image&lt;a class="anchor" href="#build-an-image"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This guide builds the image of a &lt;code&gt;builtin:container&lt;/code&gt; step from a Dockerfile in your project, then runs it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="build-from-a-dockerfile"&gt;Build from a Dockerfile&lt;a class="anchor" href="#build-from-a-dockerfile"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Replace &lt;code&gt;image&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;build&lt;/code&gt;. Set exactly one of the two.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;./api&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A relative &lt;code&gt;context&lt;/code&gt; is relative to the project directory. The step builds &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt; in the context.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="choose-a-dockerfile-arguments-and-stage"&gt;Choose a Dockerfile, arguments, and stage&lt;a class="anchor" href="#choose-a-dockerfile-arguments-and-stage"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-cue" data-lang="cue"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;builtin:container&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;./api&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dockerfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;Dockerfile.dev&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;GO_VERSION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;1.25&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;dev&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;dockerfile&lt;/code&gt; is relative to &lt;code&gt;context&lt;/code&gt;. Each entry in &lt;code&gt;args&lt;/code&gt; is a build argument.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>